<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Wpath (230)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>wpath &lt;someone or something&gt;
wpath &lt;unit@zone&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>wpath Gnort
</pre>
<p>Finds the way to someone or something: anyone or anything in the world 
by name, or a unit by its symbolic name. You are told its symbolic name, 
the room it is in (click it to goto there), and the first direction to 
walk from where you stand to get there along the shortest path. Instead 
of a direction it may say enter or exit (go into or out of something on 
the way), here, try again (the way is still being worked out: ask again 
in a moment), or impossible: there is no way both there and back, as 
across a one-way exit, or to a room made since the last reboot (new 
exits aren't known until then either).
</p><p>It replaces the old path command. It is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Goto</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Track</a>
</pre>




</div>